    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. When a player is aiming for a very pure, focused tone, are there specific overtones that they might inadvertently emphasize that change that \"airy\" quality, or does it mostly come down to air velocity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While air velocity significantly impacts overall sound production, a player aiming for purity might inadvertently emphasize specific overtones through embouchure adjustments. Too much tension can over-excite certain higher partials, leading to a shriller or more nasal character rather than a smooth, focused tone. Achieving a very pure sound relies on carefully managing the excitation to ensure the initial energy is concentrated around the fundamental, which the air column naturally favors when played correctly.",
      "source": "target",
